      {
        "id": 57468,
        "name": "Zalrus9",
        "username": "Zalrus9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/zalrus9/{size}/2124_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-04-03T16:03:41.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I've said this before, and I'll say it again, The Scholar's deck is pretty good, for many of the reasons already mentioned on this thread. I also like healing as a way to do damage; I don't really know how that works thematically, but it probably involves balls of energy, and I am ALL for that.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Although he's not my favorite villian to play, Iron Legacy's art is so heartbreaking. I remember playing him solo and listening to Isreal's \"Over the Rainbow/What a Wonderful World\" and the dissonance I felt was pretty powerful. The discarded picture.... that's rough.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:32:48.447Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
